  "reason": "The current best configuration is config_037 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) at 0.706 acc. The only untested variation of this top-performing combination is the aggregation method: transformer vs. avgpool. Prior evidence shows avgpool > transformer with weaker encoders (pca_n2000+resnet50: 0.619 vs 0.579), but this is a single data point from a less expressive feature space. With scvi_n200 and imagenet_vit_l producing richer, higher-dimensional representations, a transformer aggregation could potentially capture inter-profile interactions that simple averaging misses. Testing config_039 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) directly extends the best configuration along the most uncertain remaining axis. If it matches or exceeds 0.706, we gain a better model; if it underperforms, we confirm avgpool is the correct aggregation for this encoder pair and can focus remaining budget on other dimensions. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it resolves the last untested design choice within the proven best encoder combination."
}

